course: dictionary
lesson: 7467
title: Animal words: porcupine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A porcupine is a large rodent covered in long sharp spines called quills, which protect it from enemies. A word like porcupine can be explained in a text by the words that come after it. «Porcupines cannot shoot their quills; the quills come off easily when touched and stick into the attacker.» The clue is "cannot shoot", so quills are not thrown. They stay in the body of the animal that touched them.
explain: The sentence also tells you what a porcupine does first. «A porcupine rattles its quills and stamps its feet as a warning first.» A warning comes before the quills stick, so a porcupine would rather you stopped than got hurt. Always ask yourself what the animal is trying to do.
explain: Writers also use porcupine to describe people. If someone is prickly as a porcupine, they are grumpy, and it is hard to get close to them. The word means more than the animal, so read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: A porcupine is a large rodent with long sharp spines called quills.
fact: «Quills» are long, stiff, sharp spines that protect a porcupine from enemies.
fact: Porcupines live in two main groups: tree-climbing porcupines in the Americas, and ground-living porcupines in Africa, Asia and southern Europe.
fact: «Prickly as a porcupine» is a phrase that means grumpy or hard to get close to.
fact: A porcupine cannot shoot its quills; they come out easily when touched and stick into the attacker.
exercise: «Porcupines cannot shoot their quills; the quills come off easily when touched and stick into the attacker.» What happens when an attacker touches a porcupine's quills? | The attacker gets a warm blanket | *The quills stick into the attacker | The quills fly through the air to the attacker | The porcupine shoots the attacker with a dart
exercise: «A North American porcupine has about 30,000 quills.» What is a quill? | A soft feather | *A long sharp spine | A kind of tree | A small fish
exercise: Which porcupines are tree-climbing porcupines? | Porcupines in southern Europe | Porcupines in Africa | Porcupines in Asia | *Porcupines in the Americas
test: Ella says her brother is as prickly as a porcupine. What does she mean? | He never sleeps at night | *He is grumpy and hard to get close to | He is very good at climbing trees | He loves to be hugged
test: «A porcupine rattles its quills and stamps its feet as a warning first.» Why does it do this? | A porcupine sings a loud song | To cool down on a hot day | To find a mate in the forest | *To warn an enemy before the quills stick
exam: «The American and the African and Asian porcupines are only distant relatives, and many scientists think they grew quills separately.» Why might scientists think these porcupines grew quills separately? | They live in the same burrow | They eat the same food every day | They were born on the same day | *They are only distant relatives
